# Snap & Sync — Implementation Plan v2

> Turn a v0 mock UI into a production-ready, offline-first Expo mobile EMR app.

---

## 1. Gap Analysis — Mock vs. Production

### What the Mock Has ✅

| Area | Details |
|------|---------|
| **UI Screens** | Dashboard, Active Session, QR Scanner dialog, Manual ID Entry, Camera viewfinder, Image preview, AI spinner, Real-time AI review (split-screen), Saved flash, Review Queue (list + detail), History |
| **Navigation** | 3-tab bottom nav: Home, Queue, History |
| **Data Models** | [ExtractedField](file:///e:/patient-data-flow/lib/mock-data.ts#3-8), [PatientRecord](file:///e:/patient-data-flow/lib/mock-data.ts#9-22), [HistoryEntry](file:///e:/patient-data-flow/lib/mock-data.ts#25-34) TypeScript interfaces |
| **Flow Logic** | Session start → capture → online branch (analyze → review → approve) vs. offline branch (queue + toast) |
| **Confidence UI** | Color-coded badges/bars (<80% destructive, 80-89% primary, ≥90% success), editable fields |

### What Is Missing 🔴

| Gap | Priority | Notes |
|-----|----------|-------|
| **React Native / Expo** | Critical | Currently Next.js 16 web-only |
| **Real Camera** | Critical | Fake HTML viewfinder → needs `expo-camera` |
| **Real QR Scanner** | Critical | Simulated with `setTimeout` → needs barcode scanning |
| **Image Compression** | High | Need **tunable 150-200KB** compressed JPEG (not 50KB — too destructive for handwriting) |
| **Original Photo Retention** | High | Always save full-res original locally so doctor can review the image even before AI runs |
| **SQLite (Local DB)** | Critical | Zero local persistence |
| **Network Detection** | Critical | `isOnline` is a toggle button, not real |
| **Supabase Backend** | Critical | No auth, no DB, no storage |
| **Gemini AI Integration** | Critical | Extraction results are hardcoded mock data |
| **Optimistic UI** | High | Online AI flow must NOT block the doctor with a 10s spinner — use "Saved! AI processing in background…" pattern |
| **Background Sync** | High | No sync logic exists |
| **Authentication** | High | Doctor name hardcoded |
| **Patient Registry** | Medium | No QR → patient lookup |
| **Error Handling** | High | No error boundaries, no retry logic |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Three critical design decisions incorporated from review:**
> 1. **Compression = 150-200KB** (tunable via `COMPRESSION_TARGET_KB`), not 50KB. Gemini needs legible ink edges.
> 2. **Original photo always saved** to device filesystem immediately. Doctors can visually review their own photo at any time, even before AI extraction.
> 3. **Optimistic UI for online mode**: Doctor sees "Saved! AI is processing in background…" and can immediately capture the next page. AI results arrive async and appear as a confirmable notification — no 10-second blocking spinner.

---
//'State Management (Zustand): As the app gets complex (handling sessions, online status, and sync queues across different screens), passing props will get messy. I strongly recommend telling the AI to use Zustand. It is lightweight, much simpler than Redux, and AI agents write it perfectly.'

## 2. Architecture & Data Model

### System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Mobile ["📱 Expo App (Offline-First)"]
        UI["React Native UI"]
        SQLite["SQLite Local DB"]
        Camera["expo-camera"]
        FS["Local Filesystem<br/>(originals + compressed)"]
        NetInfo["NetInfo"]
        SyncWorker["Background Sync Worker"]
    end

    subgraph Cloud ["☁️ Supabase"]
        Auth["Auth"]
        DB["PostgreSQL"]
        Storage["Storage (Images)"]
        EdgeFn["Edge Functions"]
    end

    subgraph AI ["🤖 Gemini"]
        GeminiAPI["Gemini 2.5 Flash Vision"]
    end

    UI --> Camera
    Camera --> FS
    FS --> SQLite
    NetInfo --> SyncWorker
    SyncWorker --> Storage
    SyncWorker --> EdgeFn
    EdgeFn --> GeminiAPI
    EdgeFn --> DB
    UI -- "Online: Optimistic Save + BG AI" --> EdgeFn
```

### Supabase PostgreSQL Schema

```sql
CREATE TABLE clinics (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  name TEXT NOT NULL, location TEXT,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE doctors (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id),
  full_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  clinic_id UUID REFERENCES clinics(id),
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE patients (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  patient_code TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,  -- "AHM-924"
  full_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  date_of_birth DATE, gender TEXT CHECK (gender IN ('M','F','Other')),
  clinic_id UUID REFERENCES clinics(id),
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE sessions (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  patient_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES patients(id),
  doctor_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES doctors(id),
  started_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL, ended_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  status TEXT CHECK (status IN ('active','completed')) DEFAULT 'active',
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE records (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  session_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES sessions(id),
  image_url TEXT,                    -- Supabase Storage path
  extracted_data JSONB,
  overall_confidence FLOAT, prediction_score FLOAT,
  status TEXT CHECK (status IN ('pending_sync','pending_extraction',
    'needs_review','approved')) DEFAULT 'pending_sync',
  flagged_reason TEXT,
  doctor_corrections JSONB,
  synced_at TIMESTAMPTZ, extracted_at TIMESTAMPTZ, reviewed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);
```

### SQLite Local Schema

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, patient_code TEXT NOT NULL,
  patient_name TEXT, doctor_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  started_at TEXT NOT NULL, ended_at TEXT,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'active', synced INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS records (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, session_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  original_image_path TEXT NOT NULL,   -- full-res original (always kept)
  compressed_image_path TEXT,          -- 150-200KB version for upload
  extracted_data TEXT, overall_confidence REAL,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending_sync',
  flagged_reason TEXT, doctor_corrections TEXT,
  created_at TEXT NOT NULL, synced_at TEXT,
  FOREIGN KEY (session_id) REFERENCES sessions(id)
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sync_queue (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  record_id TEXT NOT NULL, action TEXT NOT NULL,
  retry_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0, last_attempt TEXT,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending',
  FOREIGN KEY (record_id) REFERENCES records(id)
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS patients (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, patient_code TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  full_name TEXT NOT NULL, date_of_birth TEXT, gender TEXT,
  synced INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);
```

