### Phase 2: Camera & QR Integration

#### Task 2.1 — QR Code Scanner
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 2.1:

Build /components/QrScanner.tsx using expo-camera barcode scanning.
Full-screen camera with scan-frame overlay (corner brackets, animated line).
On QR detected: extract patient_code, call onScanSuccess(code).
After 5s with no detection: show "QR Damaged? Enter ID Manually" fallback
with /components/ManualIdEntry.tsx (modal, uppercase TextInput, max 7 chars).
Handle camera permissions with useCameraPermissions().
Wire into Home tab "Start New Session" button.
Mark Task 2.1 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

#### Task 2.2 — Document Camera
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 2.2:

Build /components/DocumentCamera.tsx: camera with document-frame overlay,
instruction text, circular shutter button. On capture: takePictureAsync({
quality: 0.8, base64: false }).

Build /components/ImagePreview.tsx: show captured photo, contextual text
(online vs offline), Retake + Confirm buttons.

CRITICAL: On capture, ALWAYS save the original full-resolution photo to the
app's document directory immediately (before any compression). This is the
doctor's visual reference even when offline and AI hasn't run yet.

Wire into Active Session "Capture" button.
Mark Task 2.2 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

#### Task 2.3 — Image Compression (Tunable)
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 2.3:

Create /services/imageCompression.ts:

Define a tunable constant at the top:
  export const COMPRESSION_TARGET_KB = 180; // tune between 150-200KB

Export compressImage(uri): resize to max 1600px width, JPEG quality 0.6.
If result > COMPRESSION_TARGET_KB * 1.1, reduce quality by 0.05 and retry
(max 3 retries). Return { uri, base64, sizeKB }.

The original photo is NEVER overwritten — compression produces a separate file.
Both paths are stored in SQLite (original_image_path + compressed_image_path).
Mark Task 2.3 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

