### Phase 5: Gemini AI Integration

#### Task 5.1 — Gemini API Client
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 5.1:

Create /services/geminiService.ts:
- extractHandwriting(imageBase64): call Gemini 2.5 Flash Vision.
  System prompt instructs return of JSON: { fields: [{ label, value,
  confidence }], overallConfidence, predictionScore }.
  Illegible fields get "(?)". Parse response JSON.
  On parse failure: return { error: true, confidence: 0 }.
  Timeout: 15 seconds.

Define types in /lib/types.ts: ExtractionResult, ExtractionField.
GEMINI_API_KEY via expo-constants env var.
Mark Task 5.1 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

#### Task 5.2 — Online Flow (Optimistic UI)
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 5.2:

CRITICAL DESIGN: Do NOT block the doctor with a 10-second spinner.

Online capture flow:
1. Doctor confirms photo → immediately show "✅ Saved! AI is analyzing
   in the background…" flash with a subtle progress indicator
2. Save the record to SQLite (status='pending_extraction')
3. Compress + upload to Supabase Storage in background
4. Call Gemini API in background
5. When AI result arrives:
   a. If confidence ≥ 80%: auto-approve, update record, show a small
      in-app notification "AI verified: Amoxicillin 500mg ✓"
   b. If confidence < 80%: show a pop-up card asking doctor to review
      the extracted data (editable fields + approve button)
   c. Doctor can dismiss and review later from the Queue tab
6. Meanwhile, the doctor can IMMEDIATELY capture the next photo or
   end the session — they are never blocked.

Fallback: if API fails/timeout → silently save for offline queue.
Mark Task 5.2 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

#### Task 5.3 — Offline Flow & Background Extraction
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 5.3:

Create Supabase Edge Function /supabase/functions/extract-handwriting:
- Input: { record_id }
- Download image from Storage, call Gemini API (server-side GEMINI_API_KEY)
- Save extracted_data + confidence to records table
- If confidence < 80: status='needs_review', flagged_reason=explanation
- If confidence ≥ 80: status='approved'

Update cloudSync.ts: after image upload, call the Edge Function.

Update Review Queue: fetch records where status='needs_review' from
Supabase (replace mock data). On doctor submit: update corrections,
set status='approved'. Auto-refresh on sync completion.

IMPORTANT: Original photos are always viewable from local storage.
Doctor can tap any queued/synced record to see the high-res original.
Mark Task 5.3 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

#### Task 5.4 — History, Analytics & Final Polish
```
Read PLAN.md. Implement Task 5.4:

Wire History tab to real data:
- Online: fetch today's records from Supabase (join sessions + patients)
- Offline: fall back to local SQLite
- Derive status: ai-realtime / auto-synced / doctor-reviewed

Wire Dashboard stats: todayCount, pendingCount, aiAccuracy.

Add pull-to-refresh on all list screens.
Add haptic feedback (expo-haptics): light on QR success, medium on
shutter, success on approve.
Add loading skeletons for data-fetching screens.

Test full E2E:
- Online: QR → session → capture → optimistic save → bg AI → confirm → history
- Offline: QR → session → capture → local save → reconnect → sync →
  extraction → review queue → verify → history
Mark Task 5.4 as DONE in PLAN.md.
```

